<h2 id="timeline">Timeline</h2>

<p>Standard and Full Crawl audits are delivered within 4 business days. Enterprise audits take up to 10 business days on sites over 5,000 pages or JavaScript-heavy frameworks. The crawl and analysis simply take longer to run at that scale. Every engagement includes a walkthrough call to cover the fix list in priority order.</p>

<h2 id="faq">FAQ</h2>

<h3>What does a technical SEO audit service check?</h3>
<p>Crawlability, indexation, site architecture, speed and Core Web Vitals, and structured data. On-page content and backlinks are covered separately in the full <a href="/seo-audit-services/">SEO audit service</a>.</p>

<h3>Do I need a technical audit if my content is already good?</h3>
<p>Yes. Technical problems block Google from crawling or indexing pages no matter how strong the content is — no amount of content improvement fixes a crawl blocker.</p>

<h3>How is this different from an automated crawler tool?</h3>
<p>An automated tool flags issues without judging their severity or root cause. This service adds a senior analyst who separates real problems from tool noise and orders the fix list by actual traffic impact.</p>

<h3>Do you fix the issues you find?</h3>
<p>No. The service covers diagnosis and a prioritised fix list written clearly enough for any developer to implement. Implementation is available as a separate engagement on request.</p>

